    "lesson": {
      "title": "Pendulum swing",
      "instruction": "How do length and starting angle change a pendulum’s swing?",
      "explanation": "Ideal rigid-rod pendulum released at rest, starting angle 0–90°. No friction or air resistance.\nNonlinear motion solves θ″=−(g/L)sinθ using the elliptic time coordinate. The calculated period is 4√(L/g)K(sin(amplitude/2)); motion is independent of frame rate. Changing length, gravity or starting angle restarts the run.\nComparisons use shared gravity and initial amplitude. Length is the independent variable."
    },
